From 601487d467f92cb2553e4ea9bd8044cccc389e09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 22:19:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Smoothing: XML-only, in the config hash; validity and
 cross_quad checks; hash-stamped FC-adaptive artifacts

- Remove --smooth-systs, --smooth-systs-list and --no-smooth-systs; smooth= in
  the XML is the only control.
- Include nonzero smooth= widths in PROconfig::CalcHash, so changing smoothing
  invalidates process outputs like any other XML change (smooth="0" leaves the
  hash unchanged).
- FillSpline: refuse smoothed ratios that are NaN/inf or newly negative.
- Reject smooth= on spline_cross_quad members at XML parse time.
- PE bank (v3) and brazil archive (v2) store the config hash; save/load take the
  PROconfig and every load verifies it. Older files load with a warning, or are
  refused if the XML uses smooth=. init-bank / brazil refuse to overwrite an
  existing file that fails the check.
